  "correction_append_exact": {
    "W-SSC-118": " W02 specifies the Euclidean gauge group G, with A a Lie(G)-valued connection and F_A its curvature; these role carriers are source statements alongside the two separately qualified action expressions.",
    "W-SSC-119": " The source explicitly contrasts arbitrary Lie G-valued equivariant gauge forms on a principal G-bundle P over M with the metric-defined orthonormal/spin frame bundle. Its extra canonical theta is an R4-valued one-form on the frame bundle, sending a tangent vector at a frame to that vector's coordinates relative to the frame; this map role is absent from generic internal gauge bundles.",
    "W-SSC-120": " W02 specifically attributes this construction to Hitchin [11]: the distinguished-imaginary-time Clifford basis element yields the modified Euclidean Dirac operator, the connection space is identified with Dirac operators, and Hitchin's hyperkahler quotient gives (in his case ANTI)-self-dual connections; none are promoted as W-original mathematical authority.",
    "W-SSC-129": " For conventional real-form continuation W02 prints the Lorentz Hermiticity condition inverse(Omega_R)=adjoint(Omega_L), but the Euclidean group restriction is Omega_L and Omega_R in SU(2) together with x0 PURELY IMAGINARY; under Lorentz-covariant Wightman assumptions the latter yields SU(2)_L x SU(2)_R-covariant Schwinger functions. These apply to the conventional formulation, not to the proposed one-sided alternative.",
    "W-SSC-130": " The W02 van der Waerden index convention distinguishes Minkowski undotted s^A (A=1,2) from dotted conjugate s^(dot A), and in conventional COMPLEX spacetime declares undotted spinor carrier (1/2)_L tensor (0)_R versus dotted (0)_L tensor (1/2)_R; these binder/chirality roles are separate from the proposed alternative.",
    "W-SSC-131": " W02 specifically describes the proposed two-by-two complex spacetime matrices as linear maps FROM the dual of the right-handed (1/2)_R representation TO the right-handed (1/2)_R representation; its nonholomorphic expression and absence of SL(2,C)_L remain source-scoped proposal assertions.",
    "W-SSC-136": " The source specifically requires restricting Euclidean Schwinger-function reconstruction to POSITIVE IMAGINARY TIME and applying Osterwalder-Schrader reflection [5], while its Minkowski construction has no distinguished time direction but distinguishes positive from negative energy.",
    "W-SSC-137": " W02 cites earlier gravi-weak proposals [6], [7], [8] as external Minkowski-spacetime examples; it explicitly says those proposals do NOT involve Euclidean spacetime or twistor geometry. Those references are opaque source citation evidence, not imported W source semantics.",
    "W-SSC-145": " W02 additionally states that these complexified self-dual forms are THREE-complex-dimensional traceless maps from (1/2)_R to itself and identifies their carrier with the SYMMETRIC part of two copies of (1/2)_R. No conjugate is inserted into this symmetric-product expression.",
    "W-SSC-148": " The source describes curvature as an endomorphism of a SIX-dimensional two-form space split into TWO THREE-dimensional spaces, says 'This has a block diagonal form', and then says Einstein equations correspond to vanishing of OFF-DIAGONAL blocks, citing [14]/[13]. Preserve both pieces of wording and their possible source-scope tension without normalization or silently declaring one implication.",
    "W-SSC-151": " W02 further describes Standard Model QFT as not well-defined on Minkowski spacetime WITHOUT FURTHER INFORMATION, with analytic continuation from Euclidean spacetime one proposed route; this is the author's assessment, not a separately proved theorem. It expressly leaves reproducing observed electroweak SU(2)_L interactions as an OPEN question requiring further investigation."
  },
